  id: ram_ddr3
  displayName: Memory (DDR3 RAM)
  category: 2
  icon: {fileID: 0}
  mlLabel:
  mlAliases: []
  specChips:
  - DDR3
  - 8 GB
  - 1600 MT/s
  shortDescription: Older memory, from before DDR4. Shown to practice spotting incompatible
    parts.
  whatItDoes: DDR3 was the standard desktop memory before DDR4. It is slower, runs
    at a higher voltage, has fewer pins and its notch sits in another place again,
    so it only fits DDR3 motherboards.
  keyFacts:
  - Only fits DDR3 motherboards
  - Not compatible with DDR4 or DDR5 boards
  - 240 pins (DDR4 and DDR5 have 288)
  - Runs at 1.5 V (DDR4 1.2 V, DDR5 1.1 V)
